  "notes": "The issue set up an evaluation of whether the coordinator saves to the right place (trip brief, itinerary, or memory), then changed the instructions and measured the change. It grew from 840 words to 7,042 over 41 versions, and most of the growth came after the first PR (2026-11-10), as each of nine PRs finished a step and its status and results were written back into Do. Task is 42% of the body, but results are 30%, mostly tables and run numbers placed inside Do (I209-33 to I209-36, I209-49 to I209-56), plus status lines such as I209-28 and I209-48. The answers under the eight struck questions are all repeated in Do, so the struck text is history (I209-17 to I209-24). Most PR descriptions copied the Do step they covered; the new text in them is Joe's chat asks quoted as the task (P287-d1, P289-d1, P291-d3), and the last PR's list of what it changed (P297-d1 to d5). One copy differs from the final issue, so the issue was edited after (P294-d3 vs I209-46). The decisions comments hold 56 decisions; 23 say where they were written, mostly evals/saving/decisions.md and DEVELOPMENT.md section 5, and the #295 and #297 comments name no doc for any of their 20. Surprising: Do still says to make smaller changes if runs fail (I209-59), while the ending block says none follow (I209-57)."
